  "body": "In the steps for [scrolling a fragment identifier into view](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#scroll-to-the-fragment-identifier), there are different scroll steps for “top of document” and other fragment identifiers. In particular, we only perform [scroll into view](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#scroll-an-element-into-view) (and thus scroll ancestor viewports) in the non- top of document case. Is this intended, or what should the correct behavior be here? See http://crbug.com/545965 which addresses an interesting case - if an iframe links to # or #top, should the main document be scrolled as well at all (i.e. scroll the iframe into view, Chrome's current behavior)?\r\n\r\n@domenic I'd appreciate your thoughts here!",
